text: ['At the beginning of the end step, if you control no creatures, sacrifice Thran Quarry.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1.', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nSacrifice Shard Phoenix: It deals 2 damage to each creature without flying.\\n{R}{R}{R}: Return Shard Phoenix from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Flying\\nMenace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\nTwo-Headed Dragon can block an additional creature each combat.\\n{1}{R}: Two-Headed Dragon gets +2/+0 until end of turn.", 'Haste\\nWhenever Slith Firewalker deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', "Other Elf creatures get +1/+1 and have forestwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Other Goblin creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Regenerate another target Goblin.', "Other Merfolk get +1/+1 and have islandwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Protection from black\\nAt the beginning of each end step, if Whirling Dervish dealt damage to an opponent this turn, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Protection from red\\nShadow (This creature can block or be blocked by only creatures with shadow.)', 'Sacrifice Sakura-Tribe Elder: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "Serra Avatar's power and toughness are each equal to your life total.\\nWhen Serra Avatar is put into a graveyard from anywhere, shuffle it into its owner's library.", 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Volcanic Hammer deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Whenever City of Brass becomes tapped, it deals 1 damage to you.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'White creatures get +1/+1.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Elvish Lyrist: Destroy target enchantment.', '{T}: Destroy target tapped creature.']
flavor: ['"Enter this palace-gate and ask the news Of greatness fallen into dust and clay."\\n—*The Arabian Nights*, trans. Burton', '"In Rath," the priest said, "there is even greater need for prayer."', '"Make me thy lyre, even as the forest is: What if my leaves are falling like its own!"\\n—Percy Bysshe Shelley,\\n"Ode to the West Wind"', '"We\'ve endured your slights to Gaea with the grace of tolerance. Now behold the grace of our ferocity."', 'A master of tactics, the Lord of Atlantis makes his people bold in battle merely by arriving to lead them.', 'Amid this whirling hurricane of blades, there is no calm eye in which the hapless can find shelter.', "Cast the weight as though it were a die, to see a rival's fate.", 'One part cunning, one part wise, and many, many parts demented.', "The slith incubate in the Great Furnace's heat, emerging on Mirrodin's surface only when the four suns have aligned overhead.", 'The songs of angels are perceived not as words in the ears but as stirrings in the soul.', 'There were no tombstones in orochi territory. Slain warriors were buried with a tree sapling, so they would become a part of the forest after death.', 'Trained in the arts of stealth, royal assassins choose their victims carefully, relying on timing and precision rather than brute force.']
artist: ['Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Christopher Rush', 'Dany Orizio', 'Dermot Power', 'Justin Sweet', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Melissa A. Benson', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Ron Spencer', 'Sam Wood', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Wayne Reynolds']
